Subject: [TEST builds only] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: let pcie_0_gdsc collapse in system suspend, but not under a host that keeps its link

Test builds only.  scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh applies this only with
APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_OFF=1, after gcc-sm8550-usb-gdscs-retention.patch,
refuses it without APPLY_SM8550_SLEEP_FIXES=1 and without the guard's other
half, APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_GUARD=1 (below), and refuses a build without
the variable in a source tree that carries it.  No board check: both
tablets' builds get it when the variable is set.

Two lines of pcie_0_gdsc's entry, in one hunk:
  - .pwrsts goes from PWRSTS_RET_ON to PWRSTS_OFF_ON.  gdsc_disable() then
    drops the application processor's vote for it (it is VOTABLE, and probe
    clears GDSC_SLEEP_ENA_VOTE) when genpd powers it off at the end of a
    suspend's noirq phase, instead of leaving it on in hardware until CX
    collapses;
  - its genpd gets GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP: genpd then does not power it
    off at all for a device of it that is on the awake path at the end of
    its noirq suspend, and does not power it on again at the resume, since
    it never went off (genpd_finish_suspend() and genpd_finish_resume(),
    drivers/pmdomain/core.c, the flag's only readers; gdsc_init() and
    pm_genpd_init() add to pd.flags and keep what is there).  The domain's
    one device is the PCIe host 1c00000.pcie, which
    pcie-qcom-keep-power-domain-while-link-kept.patch, the guard's other
    half, puts on the awake path when it keeps its link through the
    suspend, and marks out-of-band when it powered itself down (genpd then
    powers the domain off whatever the endpoints' wakeup settings put on
    the awake path).
So the domain collapses in a suspend in which the PCIe host has powered
itself down, and stays on in one in which the host keeps its link.  Nothing
else changes: pcie_0_phy_gdsc, the PCIe1 domains and the USB domains keep
their states.  The file gets one line more, so the debug switches go in one
line further down with this patch than without it.  The compiled .data of
gcc-sm8550.o differs from the build without this patch in two bytes,
pcie_0_gdsc's .pwrsts (6 to 5) and its pd.flags (0 to 8).  Both are in the
table, which keeps clang's order of the GDSC objects in .data: the same
flag set from the probe or from the init function moved pcie_0_gdsc there
(tried on a scratch build).

Why the collapse.  On the SM-X710 (gts9wifi) a sleep with the PCIe host
powered down (its root port removed, so that dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() takes
its power-off branch) and the interconnect floor released did not return
with this GDSC in retention: 0 of 8 (six on Type-C kit revision 7's kernel,
one on revision 9's, one on revision 10's), the SoC dropping PS_HOLD 43 to
44 s after the RTC alarm; the same sleep with the floor held came back.
With the GDSC collapsed it returned 7 of 7 (four on revision 9, three on
revision 10, through the run-time switch of
gcc-sm8550-gdsc-debug-switches.patch), and with revision 10's PIPE clock
revert the PCIe host came back as well.  Two SM8550 community kernels with
the same symptom made the domain PWRSTS_OFF_ON (ROCKNIX PR 3636,
retroforge patch 0143).

Why not under a host that keeps its link (upstream's reason for
PWRSTS_RET_ON, 967e011013ed, "clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: Do not turn off PCIe
GDSCs during gdsc_disable()", v6.14): a PCIe controller that keeps its link
through a system suspend (qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() with the link kept, the
PCI devices still bound) loses its registers when its GDSC collapses, and
its resume breaks.  That is the case on this port in every suspend in which
the Wi-Fi stays: the root port cannot go to D3, so dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()
keeps the link.  The boot's pm_test=platform panel cycle is such a suspend.
Without the guard (kit revision 11 as first prepared) genpd collapsed the
domain in it.

The cost of the guard: while the link is kept the domain stays on, and with
it its parent's vote: CX's genpd stays on (the domain's subdomain count),
and rpmhpd votes CX at its enable level (retention) or above in every set
(rpmhpd_power_on(), rpmhpd_set_performance_state()), where genpd could
otherwise vote it 0 under a live controller.  A live host has no use for a
collapsed CX.

It needs the PIPE clock revert (clk-qcom-regmap-phy-mux-revert-rework.patch,
APPLY_SM8550_SLEEP_FIXES=1): without it the GDSC did not report power-up at
the resume ("pcie_0_gdsc status stuck at 'off'", revision 9).

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3003,7 +3003,8 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
+		.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON, /* gcc-sm8550-pcie0-gdsc-off-in-suspend.patch */
 	.flags = VOTABLE | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };

